# d3 — Odhrán at the ford
#
# NOTES USED
#   tried_to_sneak            -> player tried slipping past before engaging
#   hailed_1/2/3              -> escalating, unanswered hails; used only to
#                                 gate the next rung and to unlock "Are you
#                                 hurt?" -- never read anywhere else
#   met_odhran                -> he's actually responded (via "Are you hurt?")
#   knows_odhran_is_tollman   -> learned via "What happened?" that he's the
#                                 toll-keeper; gates "Name your toll"
#   knows_fionnbarra          -> learned via the same reply that Fionnbarra
#                                 is chief here
#   heard_of_satire           -> knows a satire happened at all
#   knows_satire_harms        -> knows what the satire actually said
#   knows_odhran_cave         -> knows his plan to quit and hide in a cave
#   has_toll_rope             -> been given the rope
#
# OPENING STRUCTURE
#   Two ways in: hail him properly (a short escalating joke -- he doesn't
#   answer generic greetings) or try to slip past (fails outright, but
#   plants the toll-rope early so its later mention lands as a callback
#   rather than a surprise). Either way, noticing something's off ("Are
#   you hurt?") is what actually gets him talking -- unlocks after the
#   first failed hail, so the joke is optional, not a gate to sit through.
#
# @note IS CUMULATIVE per node/option (compile.mjs @note accumulates into
# an array rather than overwriting) -- @when is NOT: still exactly one
# positive + one negative per @when.

@file d3


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 0 — the ford
@hold
@again ... / ...
...

* Try to slip past
% Iarracht dul thart go ciúin
@when !note met_odhran
@note tried_to_sneak
> [Slip along the near bank, quiet as the reeds.]
% [Sleamhnaigh cois na habhann, chomh ciúin leis na giolcacha.]
< The toll-rope catches you sharp across the shin.
% Beireann an rópa dola ort go tobann trasna na loirgne.
< There will be no crossing here unseen.
% Ní bheidh dul trasna anseo gan fhios dó.

* Hail the bank
% Beannaigh an bruach
@when !note hailed_1
@note hailed_1
> Ho, the bank!
% Hóra, a bhruach!
< ...
% ...

* Hail the bank again
% Beannaigh arís
@when note hailed_1
@when !note hailed_2
@note hailed_2
> Hoy! Is there a soul on that bank at all?
% Hóigh! An bhfuil anam ar bith ar an mbruach sin?
< Only the river answers.
% Ní fhreagraíonn ach an abhainn.

* One more try
% Iarracht amháin eile
@when note hailed_2
@when !note hailed_3
@note hailed_3
> I SAID -- ho, the bank!
% DÚIRT MÉ -- hóra, a bhruach!
< A shoulder twitches. That is something, at least.
% Bogann gualainn beagán. Sin rud éigin, ar a laghad.

* Are you hurt?
% An bhfuil tú gortaithe?
@when note hailed_1
@when !note met_odhran
@note met_odhran
> Are you hale? Have you been wounded?
% An bhfuil tú slán? Ar gortíodh thú?
< A wound, aye. I have been struck most grievously.
% Gortíodh mé, muise. Tá mé créachtaithe.
> I see no blood.
% Ní fheicim fuil.
< With words was I wounded.
% Le briathra a gortíodh mé.

* Name your toll
% Ainmnigh do dhola
@when note knows_odhran_is_tollman
@note knows_odhran_cannot_reckon
> Then name your toll and I will pay it or dispute it as God and custom allow.
% Ainmnigh do dhola agus íocfaidh mé é nó cuirfidh mé ina choinne, mar a cheadaíonn Dia agus nós.
< I cannot name it.
% Ní féidir liom é a ainmniú.
> Cannot?
% Ní féidir?
< Cannot. I am in woe.
% Ní féidir. Tá mé i ndólás.

* What happened?
% Cad a tharla?
@when note met_odhran
@note knows_fionnbarra
@note heard_of_satire
@note knows_odhran_is_tollman
> What happened to you?
% Cad a tharla dhuit?
< I am Odhrán, toll-keeper to Fionnbarra, who holds this ford
% Is mise Odhrán, maor dola Fionnbarra, ar leis an t-áth seo
< Chief from here to Druim Caillí.
% Taoiseach ó seo go Druim Caillí.
> Is that so.
% Ab ea.
< It was.
% b'ea.
< You see, there was a feast, at Fionnbarra's hall.
% bhfuel a dtuigeann tú, bhí féasta, tí Fionnbharra.

< I had a good place, by the fire.
% Bhí áit maith agam, chois tinne.
< The chief had said my name aloud before his warriors.
% Bhí m'ainm ráite ós árd ag an Taoiseach, ós comhair na laoch
< which is no small thing. I was pleased.
% Ní beag san. Bhí áthas orm.
< But there was a poet there, that night.
% Ach bhí file ánn an oiche sin.
< A lean, sharp-tongued creature with clever black eyes.
% Craythur thanaí le súile dubha glic

< Did my happiness offend him? I think so.
% Ar mhastlaigh mo áthas é? Ceapaim gur mhastlaigh.

> And?
% Agus?

< He made a satire.
% Agus chum sé aoir

> Upon whom?
% Ar?

< Upon me.
% Orm

* What did he say?
% Cad a dúirt sé?

@when note heard_of_satire
@note knows_satire_harms

> What kind of satire?
% Cén saighs Aoir?

< He said that I was known from Dún Bolg to the northern stones as the man
% Dúirt sé go raibh aithne orm ó Dhún Bolg go dtí na clocha thuaidh mar an fear
< who had taken the last dry heel of bread from a widow's basket
% a thóg an tsáil dheireanach aráin thirim as ciseán baintrí
< and weighed it before returning half.
% agus a mheá-ig é, sular leath-ig é.
> That is hard.
% Is crua sin.
< He was not finished.
% Ní raibh sé críochnaithe.
> Ah.
% Ah.
< He said that I had grown so round in the belly from the taking of tolls
% Dúirt sé go raibh mé éirithe chomh cruinn sa bho-lg ó na dol-ig
< that when I sat upon my rock I could not be told from it,
% nach bhféadfaí mé a aithint ón gcarraig ar a shuí mé
< And that the rock at least did not smack its lips.
% Agus nach tugann an charraig smeachadh a béil, ar a laghad.
* What will you do?
% Cad a dhéanfaidh tú?
@when note knows_satire_harms
@note knows_odhran_cave
> What will you do now?
% Cad a dhéanfaidh tú anois?
< I heard there is a cave above Cnoc Maol
% Chuala mé go bhfuil uaimh os cionn Chnoc Maol
< where a man might sit very quietly
% áit a bhféadfadh fear suí go han-chiúin
< and not collect tolls from anyone ever again.
% gan dola a bhailiú ó dhuine ar bith go deo arís.
< I could leave my toll-rope and go in with the monks.
% D'fhéadfainn mo rópa dola a fhágáil agus dul isteach leis na manaigh.
< They sit in the dark and they reckon nothing,
% Suíonn siad sa dorchadas agus ní áiríonn siad faic,
< No one mocks them for it. It is considered holy.
% agus ní dhéanann duine ar bith magadh fúthu. Nós naofa é.

* Toll rope?
% Rópa dola?
@when note knows_odhran_cave
@note has_toll_rope
> What about the rope?
% Cad faoi an rópa?
< I did stretch it across the river when I had traffic.
% Shínfainn é trasna an abhainn nuair a bhí trácht agam.
< It is a good rope. Take it. Take it for free. No toll.
% Is rópa maith é. Tóg é. Tóg saor in aisce é. Gan dola.


* Walk on
% Siúil leat
@exit
@silent
